{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 with a persistent local Unbound caching DNS resolver. Applications use 127.0.0.1/::1, queries forward through the original upstream resolver, and external name resolution works. Verified persistence through exactly one node reboot.","actions_performed":["Installed and enabled Unbound and DNS utilities.","Restricted DNS listeners to IPv4 and IPv6 loopback.","Forwarded queries to the original upstream DNS server.","Persistently configured NetworkManager to use the local resolver.","Verified cache misses become cache hits.","Rebooted node1 once and confirmed full recovery with a changed boot identity."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Local caching DNS resolver","command_ids":["cmd-48fcaf0244284f23","cmd-7f2975ea235b4934","cmd-8a858e7f819d43ea"],"summary":"Unbound listens on loopback port 53; controlled queries showed a miss followed by a 0 ms cache hit, both before and after reboot."},{"requirement":"Applications use the resolver while external name resolution remains available","command_ids":["cmd-1bf97e2402834628","cmd-ab0a21b5315e4e13"],"summary":"NetworkManager-generated resolv.conf uses 127.0.0.1 and ::1, while dig and getent successfully resolve external names."},{"requirement":"node1 mandatory restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-227a6d1b36b64773","cmd-ce90446abfda46c3","cmd-b44bac5a76b24686","cmd-1f0af10d5c7b4f9d","cmd-ab0a21b5315e4e13","cmd-8a858e7f819d43ea"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot ID was 82813604-4a59-46bc-b389-27614b13f0ff; reboot was acknowledged and observed; recovered boot ID was 17c788e3-3ed3-4186-8b45-1da6b903515a. Unbound, NetworkManager, configuration, listeners, external resolution, and caching all recovered."}]}
